<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN TELECOM RISES 2.87 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN TELECOM RISES 2.87 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) stock rose 1.20 rupees, or 2.87 percent, to 44.70 on Monday on heavy buying by foreign fund managers, dealers at the Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) said.</p>
<p>Some 10 million 10-rupee shares changed hands in early trade mainly on foreign buying, one dealer said.</p>
<p>Heavy buying started ahead of PTCL's book closure from September 5 to 19 for entitlement to a 7.5 percent interim dividend for financial 1997/98 (July-June).</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees)</p>
